<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-command-surface> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Expose provider census, status, aliases and subscription-host census through one static providers command family with bounded filters, stable JSON, explicit effects and no ad hoc operational script dependency. Reserve account receipt and host census as separately graph-gated leaves behind one predecessor-owned dispatcher/help integration so later answer, qualification and parallel stages use probe, route and call without reopening shared registries." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:operator-provider-command-reservation> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:operator-provider-command-reservation> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The predecessor-owned static operator registry reserves the complete graph-known providers command tree exactly once: census, status, aliases, host census, receipt acquire and receipt verify, plus static usf doctor --provider-home ABSOLUTE_PATH help. It owns src/commands/providers.ts and one decomposed src/commands/provider-leaf-dispatch.ts boundary. Module presence and parent-process importability are never authority. Each production leaf invocation must use one fresh single-invocation Node child; the long-running parent may not import or cache a feature handler. The parent binds the selected root to its implementation root and holds the shared primary-mutation lock before the child's first repository-module load. In that fresh process the child rederives the exact explicit profile/manifest owner, current verified completion and current file-based basis, selects the unique typed ProductionLeafRuntimeClosure, canonicalizes identical path/digest rows into sorted roles, refuses missing members, conflicting digests or unknown roles, authenticates every same-root regular non-symlink member by SHA-256, imports only the declared handler and reauthenticates the entry bytes. The child then releases its shared lock and emits one bounded prepared message; the parent releases its shared lock and acknowledges; only after that acknowledgement may the handler or provider inference begin. Use exact process.execPath without a shell, scrub inherited credentials, proxies and Node mutation options, bound the control/result protocol, and allow no same-process or alternate-route fallback. Failure before or after preparation terminates the child and returns one stable refusal. Concurrent children and readers remain parallel; only cooperative primary mutation takes the exclusive lock, and inference never holds it. Confined validation uses injected authority, lock, loader and child-handshake substitutes with no real child or provider contact, including one planted shared/preloaded-module movement case. Feature packets implement only their leaf modules and never rewrite the predecessor registry, dispatcher, help, CLI or child boundary. Git and GitHub state are not authority." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
