<urn:usf:requirement:operator-composable-command-input> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:operator-composable-command-input> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Remove the measured per-argument argv ceiling from the existing call and resolve commands through one reusable local input boundary. Each command accepts exactly one of --input .usf/inputs/FILE.json, --input -, or one bounded inline JSON compatibility argument. File input is one direct child of the selected repository's ignored .usf/inputs directory: its resolved lexical absolute path must equal realpath and remain inside the same selected root; the invoking uid owns it; it is mode 0600, regular, non-symlink and nlink 1; O_NOFOLLOW is mandatory; and pre-open lstat, opened-fd fstat and post-read fstat must have identical dev, ino, size, mtime and ctime. Read incrementally through at most maximumInputBytes plus one byte so oversize is observed without unbounded allocation. Stdin and inline input use the same non-empty four-MiB application ceiling, while inline compatibility remains subject to the host shell's smaller argv ceiling and is not the large-payload path. Decode with fatal UTF-8 and parse exactly one JSON value before command logic. Call reconstructs every assignment basis with parseRealisationBasis and requires exact same-basis before its immutable no-contact core; resolve reconstructs the envelope basis and every contribution basis, requires exact same-basis, and never weakens recursive basis immutability. The registered composable call-to-resolve chain accepts only a closed schema-valid urn:usf:call-result:1 envelope with status ok, failures empty, metrics requested equal to succeeded and contributions.length, metrics failed zero, and envelope basis exactly equal to every contribution basis. Partial, refused or internally inconsistent envelopes refuse without resolving a successful subset. A legacy bare contribution array remains manual non-batch compatibility only, carries no call-batch-completeness claim and cannot evidence the registered composable chain. No-contact bootstrap call, manual resolve and candidate formation mint no construction, completion, publication or write authority; apply remains the required boundary that rederives exact current basis before any write. Every future external-contact call leaf must rederive exact current basis beneath its authenticated graph gate before leaf import or provider contact. Argument-shape, containment or size, JSON or basis, incomplete-envelope and schema failures use the declared stable refusal codes. The input reader performs no provider, network, semantic, Git, authority or tracked write effect." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
