<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-subscription-census-containment> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Require one explicit absolute operator-selected provider-state root; authenticate its real owner-controlled non-symlink boundary and each exact recognized auth file without printing or copying content. Launch only fixed absolute Codex and Claude metadata commands in independent Bubblewrap children with a tmpfs root, private user, PID and network namespaces, no host sockets or working tree, read-only system and exact auth-file projections, cleared environment, private scratch, bounded output and timeout. Exact absence of /usr/bin/codex or /usr/bin/claude is evaluated before auth-file absence and yields a route-local EXECUTABLE_NOT_FOUND observation with its frozen candidate denominator, even when that host's recognized auth file is also absent; it must not suppress an independently observable sibling host. A dangling or unsafe present host executable, unsafe provider-state root, unavailable Bubblewrap containment tool or observed containment/projection drift still refuses the census. Inability to answer without network remains unavailable and never widens this census into provider contact." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
