<urn:usf:carrier-intent:provider-pipeline-decomposition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:legacyLesson> "V2 already established affected-proof-family invalidation and coherent-batch repinning. A stated scoped-currentness rule is not implemented when one global WorkPacket chain or whole-file route input still makes sibling and run observations transitive source dependencies." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:carrier-intent:provider-pipeline-decomposition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:criticalPathRule> "Construct reusable account, invocation, evaluator, routing and parallel-runtime capabilities only from genuine code dependencies; keep route-keyed account, adapter, authorization, answer, evaluation and qualification records ignored beneath .usf and out of Git publication." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:carrier-intent:provider-pipeline-decomposition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:adoptionRule> "Use canonical keyed-member digests and exact immutable operational receipts so sibling movement and repeated calls do not stale source capabilities; provider contact requires a fresh nonreplaceable expiry-bound authorization immediately before invocation." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:carrier-intent:provider-pipeline-decomposition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:sharedRegistryRule> "Treat the one-time complete providers command-tree dispatch/help reservation as predecessor-owned operator registry integration; it reserves census, status, aliases, host census, receipt acquire and receipt verify, while provider-census owns only its feature files. Check predecessor and independent write overlap over the complete imported manifest, not one source graph. Later receipt, answer, qualification, parallel and semantic-token realization uses the already reserved providers, probe, route and call boundaries and does not rewrite the shared CLI registry." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:carrier-intent:provider-pipeline-decomposition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "This carrier does not grant provider contact, credential forwarding, account receipt trust, authenticated answers, qualification, parallelism, token reduction, Git or terminal proof." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:carrier-intent:provider-pipeline-decomposition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Observed legacy credential-name presence is import-source history only; this carrier neither copies secrets nor configures a repository-local live credential projection." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
